Within the addressable region, hardware behavior further reduces the effective output: approximately 7 pixels at the left edge of the framebuffer are not output.<ref>This loss occurs within the VI's internal fetch and resampling pipeline and is independent of analog encoding or display characteristics.</ref> Because the VI performs horizontal scaling via fixed-point arithmetic (<code>VI_X_SCALE</code>), this translates to VI output space as:

 7 × (1024 / X_SCALE)

=== Derived video timing ===

As of the time of writing (May 6, 2026), there is a known discrepancy between the [https://github.com/DragonMinded/libdragon/tree/preview preview branch of Libdragon] and all known prior definitions for PAL-M progressive signals. Currently, the Libdragon prevew branch uses Libdragon main branch's PAL-M interlaced VI register configuration for both progressive and interlaced modes, rather than the differing profiles for progressive and interlaced of Libultra and Libdragon's main branch. Thus, the following tables do not apply to software using MPAL progressive in conjunction with the Libdragon preview branch.

From VCLK, the [[Video Interface]] counts VI clocks per line (L) and half-lines per frame (S) to produce the horizontal and vertical scan frequencies.<ref>Full derivations shown in the [https://github.com/meauxdal/N64-Refresh-Rate-Reference N64 Refresh Rate Reference].</ref>

{| class="wikitable" style="text-align: center;"
! Standard !! Scan !! <math>f_H</math> (Hz) !! <math>f_V</math> (Hz)
|-
| '''NTSC''' || Progressive || <math>\frac{2{,}250{,}000}{143}</math> || <math>\frac{2{,}250{,}000}{37{,}609}</math>
|-
| '''NTSC''' || Interlaced || <math>\frac{2{,}250{,}000}{143}</math> || <math>\frac{60{,}000}{1{,}001}</math>
|-
| '''PAL''' || Progressive || <math>15{,}625</math> || <math>\frac{15{,}625}{313}</math>
|-
| '''PAL''' || Interlaced || <math>15{,}625</math> || <math>50</math>
|-
| '''MPAL''' || Progressive || <math>\frac{4{,}572{,}156{,}375{,}000}{290{,}532{,}671}</math> || <math>\frac{17{,}384{,}625{,}000}{290{,}532{,}671}</math>
|-
| '''MPAL''' || Interlaced || <math>\frac{71{,}583{,}750{,}000}{4{,}547{,}257}</math> || <math>\frac{272{,}700{,}000}{4{,}547{,}257}</math>
